### Type Safety Requirements
@type_requirements [
  {
    "id": "type_hints",
    "rule": "Use type hints for all function parameters and returns",
    "example": "def execute_swap(token_address: str, amount: float) -> Dict[str, Any]:"
  },
  {
    "id": "typed_dict",
    "rule": "Use TypedDict for API response structures",
    "example": "class SwapResponse(TypedDict): signature: str"
  },
  {
    "id": "enums",
    "rule": "Use Enum for constants like trade states",
    "example": "class TradeState(Enum): PENDING = 'pending'"
  }
]

### Async Programming Standards
- Use async/await for all I/O operations
- Implement proper timeout handling
- Use aiohttp for HTTP requests
- Handle connection pool management

### Error Handling Patterns
@error_handling [
  {
    "pattern": "custom_exceptions",
    "implementation": "Create domain-specific exceptions",
    "example": "class InsufficientLiquidityError(TradingError): pass"
  },
  {
    "pattern": "no_silent_failures",
    "implementation": "Always raise exceptions, never return None for errors",
    "severity": "critical"
  },
  {
    "pattern": "transaction_retry",
    "implementation": "Implement exponential backoff for RPC errors",
    "max_retries": 3
  }
]

### Trading Logic Standards
- Validate all token addresses before operations
- Check wallet balance before trades
- Implement slippage protection
- Log all transaction attempts with context

### API Integration Patterns
@api_patterns {
  "quicknode_metis": {
    "rate_limit": "Respect tier limits (10 RPS free)",
    "error_codes": "Handle specific Métis error responses",
    "retry_strategy": "Exponential backoff with jitter"
  },
  "solana_rpc": {
    "connection": "Use persistent connection pools",
    "confirmation": "Wait for 'confirmed' status minimum",
